<title>UK: Siebe dives as NatWest changes stance.</title>
<headline>Siebe dives as NatWest changes stance.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Siebe Plc shares plunged 21-1/2p to 972-1/2p on Friday after NatWest Markets changed its recommendation to reduce from hold, dealers said.</p>
<p>NatWest analyst John Pearson confirmed the shift in stance but declined to comment further.</p>
<p>Volume was a slim 41,368 shares traded by 0730 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
